<title>SINGAPORE: CK Tang half year net loss down 18.5 pct.</title>
<headline>CK Tang half year net loss down 18.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to September 30 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss			 7.19	vs     8.82</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)	  (17.40)     vs   (21.40)</p>
<p>    Turnover		     109.93	vs    88.95</p>
<p>    Investment income	    0.10	vs     0.11</p>
<p>    Other income		   0.80	vs     0.44</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)	   3.58	vs     1.95</p>
<p>    Pre-tax loss		   7.20	vs     8.10</p>
<p>    Associates		     nil	 vs    (0.84)</p>
<p>    Minorities		     0.01	vs     0.11</p>
<p>Note - Retail company CK Tang Ltd said it expected performance to improve in the second half as steps have been taken to re-engineer its merchandising process, maximise productivity of space and human resources and work closer with suppliers to improve profit margins.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
